    "notes": "Four sessions at Columbia 30th Street Studio, NYC: July 22 (Gone, Gone Gone Gone, My Man's Gone Now), July 29 (Bess You Is My Woman Now, Fishermen Strawberry and Devil Crab, It Ain't Necessarily So, Here Come de Honey Man), August 4 (Buzzard Song, Oh Bess Oh Where's My Bess, Prayer), August 18 (Summertime, I Wants to Stay Here, There's a Boat) (S2 session matrix numbers). Jimmy Cobb replaced Philly Joe Jones on drums from the July 29 session (S2). Jerome Richardson replaced Phil Bodner on flute from the August 4 session (S2). NOTE on session-date conflict: Wikipedia's per-track 'Recorded' column dates Summertime and There's a Boat to 8/4/58 (S1), while jazzdisco's CO-matrix evidence dates them 8/18/58 (S2); the dossier follows jazzdisco (session authority) and flags the conflict. Track durations follow the 1997 Legacy CD (CK 65141) reissue; original LP CL 1274 had 13 tracks, the CD adds the two bonus/alternate takes flagged above. Apple Music primary listing is the 15-track Legacy reissue (collectionId 282213298); a 13-track Mono Version (1225723234) also exists. AllMusic styles: Cool, Experimental Big Band, Third Stream, Trumpet Jazz (S3); Wikipedia genres: third stream, orchestral jazz, cool jazz (S1). style_primary 'cool-jazz'. Producer Cal Lampley (S1, S3); engineer Frank Laico (S1, S3). Cover design Teresa Alfieri; cover photography Roy DeCarava (S1)."
